cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this harness or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "System One Harness: a pilot on decision models as a triage gate for security research"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Heringer
    given-names: Niklas
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-11
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mev0lent/system-one-harness"
url: "https://niklas-heringer.com/research/system-one-ai-cybersecurity/"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible pilot on synthetic HTTP response triage. Four decision models (Laya, GLiNER2.5-Decide,
  Jev 1.13.0 and OpenAI's Decisions API) and three generative LLM settings act as a gate in front of an
  expensive reasoning model. Every model output is committed, and one command recomputes every number.
keywords:
  - security research
  - decision models
  - large language models
  - anomaly detection
  - calibration
  - prompt injection
  - request smuggling
